  "$comment": [
    "BRAND-ASSET QUARANTINE RECORD — Phase UI-05, defect UI01-ASSET-002.",
    "",
    "Eleven unapproved brand working files shipped inside the public web root of the production",
    "image and were publicly served. UI/UX plan §17 permits only approved brand assets there.",
    "",
    "They were MOVED, not deleted, with `git mv`, into a non-public source-controlled archive.",
    "docs/ is never copied into the nginx image, so the bytes are preserved and reviewable while",
    "being unreachable over HTTP.",
    "",
    "This file is the reviewed DECISION record, and is deliberately separate from the UI-00 source",
    "inventory: that inventory is a live statement about what is on disk, so after the move it",
    "correctly reports zero unreferenced files under the brand tree and can no longer be the",
    "authority for what was quarantined. Every hash below was verified against the UI-00 inventory",
    "BEFORE the move and re-verified from the archived bytes after it.",
    "",
    "`node scripts/generate-landing-images.mjs` verifies this record on every run: each original",
    "path must be absent from the public tree, each quarantine path must exist, and each archived",
    "file must still hash to the value recorded here.",
    "",
    "Restoring any of these to public/assets/brand/ requires product-owner approval.",
    "Approved brand assets — Logo.png, the favicons, the Android icons and site.webmanifest — were",
    "not touched, and no file was deleted.",
    "",
    "Phase UI-06 reconciliation: `closure_status` moved HERE from the generator, which hard-coded",
    "it. The lifecycle of a defect is a reviewed decision, not a generator constant — keeping the",
    "value in the generator meant promoting a merged closure required editing a build tool. The",
    "generated audit artifact now copies this field, so there is exactly one authority for it."
  ],
